    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i need some help with a cow that just had a rumenotomy done this morning. what should i be looking out for in the next 48 hours to make sure she doesn't get an infection or something? also what kind of feed can i start giving her once she's stable?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In the next 48 hours, closely monitor the surgical site for signs of infection like excessive swelling, redness, discharge, or foul odor. Watch her closely for signs of systemic problems, including fever, lethargy, or refusal to eat. Once she is stable, begin reintroducing feed slowly with easily digestible, high-energy sources, such as hay mixed with molasses or a paste-like feed. Always follow your veterinarian's specific dietary instructions as they know the details of the surgery.",
      "source": "target",
